course: medicine
lesson: 76
title: Olympiad: body numbers, clocks and scores ★★★
level: primary-4
stars: 3
explain: This olympiad block closes the course, and its first lesson hides the numbers the course taught inside puzzles: beats in a pulse, cubes of sugar, minutes under the tap, hours of sleep, days off after a head knock and points on a scoreboard.
explain: Picture Zara after the bleep test, two fingers on her wrist and an eye on the clock: she counts beats for 15 seconds, and the trick is to remember that a minute is four of those, so the number she counted is never the answer by itself.
explain: Many puzzles hide a trap in the words: a number someone corrects («30 — no wait, 25»), an aside that changes nothing, or a hyperbole like «my heart beat a million times», where the big number is a feeling, not a count.
explain: Some puzzles join two lessons, like the sugar in a can and the sugar limit for a day, or the stopping distance of a car and a kid stepping out between parked vans, and the answer only comes when both facts are put side by side.
fact: To find a pulse per minute you count the beats for 15 seconds and multiply by 4; a child's resting pulse is often about 70 to 100 and can climb to about 160 to 190 when running hard.
fact: A 330 ml can of regular cola has about 35 g of sugar, and the UK daily limit of free sugars for children aged 7 to 10 is about 24 g; one sugar cube is roughly 4 g.
fact: A burn is cooled under cool running water for 20 minutes, and a bleeding cut is pressed firmly for about 10 minutes without lifting the cloth to look.
fact: Children aged 6 to 12 need about 9 to 12 hours of sleep a night, and one sleep cycle lasts about 90 minutes.
fact: About half of the caffeine in a drink is still in the body about 5 hours later.
fact: After a concussion, UK grassroots guidance allows no competitive sport for at least 21 days.
fact: Sun cream is put on again at least every 2 hours, and after sweating hard or towelling.
fact: The Highway Code gives a stopping distance at 30 mph of about 23 m: about 9 m thinking plus 14 m braking.
fact: In rugby union a try is 5, a conversion 2 and a penalty goal 3; in cricket a ball over the boundary in the air is 6 and one that bounces first is 4; in a football league a win is 3 points and a draw 1.
fact: Children have 20 baby teeth and most have 28 adult teeth by about 13, with wisdom teeth sometimes later.
fact: Michael Phelps won 28 Olympic medals, 23 of them gold; the Summer Olympics come every 4 years, and Tokyo «2020» was held in 2021.
fact: In 2026 the men's World Cup had 48 teams in 12 groups of 4, and 32 teams went through to the knockouts; a 6 pm kick-off in Los Angeles was 2 am in the UK.
fact: For measles about 95 in every 100 people need to be immune for herd immunity.
fact: «Bleep test» is a running test between two lines that gets faster with each bleep; «proper job» in the West Country means really well done.
exercise: Zara counts 22 beats in 15 seconds. What is her pulse per minute? | 88 | 22 | 37 | 66
exercise: Leo counts 30 beats in 15 seconds — no wait, he says, it was 25. What's his pulse per minute? | 100 | 120 | 25 | 110
exercise: One can of cola has about 35 g of sugar and the daily limit is about 24 g. By how many grams does one can go over? | By about 11 g | About 59 g | About 24 g | Not at all
exercise: A sugar cube is about 4 g. About how many cubes are in two cans of cola, 35 g each? | About 18 | About 9 | About 70 | About 8
exercise: A burn goes under the cool tap at 5:50 pm. When can the cooling stop at the earliest? | 6:10 pm | 6:00 pm | 5:70 pm | 6:20 pm
exercise: Mia presses on a cut at 3:00, peeks at 3:04 and it bleeds again, so she starts over. When should she look next? | At about 3:14 | At about 3:10 | At about 3:06 | Straight away, to check
exercise: Kai needs 10 hours of sleep and his alarm for early training is at 6:30 am. When should he be asleep? | By 8:30 pm | By 9:30 pm | By 10:30 pm | By 8:00 pm
exercise: How many 90-minute sleep cycles fit into 9 hours of sleep? | 6 | 9 | 4 | 3
exercise: Ruby drinks a cola with caffeine at 4 pm. About what part of the caffeine is still in her at 9 pm? | About half | All of it, every bit | None of it at all | About a quarter
exercise: Olly gets concussion in a match on Saturday the 1st. Which is the earliest competitive match he may play? | Saturday the 22nd | Saturday the 8th | Saturday the 15th | Sunday the 2nd, if he feels fine
exercise: Sun cream goes on at 9 am on sports day and is put on again every 2 hours. How many more times by 3 pm? | 3 | 2 | 6 | 4
exercise: A driver at 30 mph needs about 23 m to stop. A boy steps out 20 m in front. What happens? | The car can't stop in time | The car stops 3 m before him | The car stops right next to him | The car stops 20 m before him
exercise: A rugby team scores 3 tries, all converted, and 1 penalty goal. How many points? | 24 | 21 | 18 | 27
exercise: A batter hits 3 sixes and 2 fours, and nothing else. How many runs? | 26 | 22 | 30 | 5
exercise: A team wins 5 games, draws 2 and loses 3. How many league points? | 17 | 15 | 10 | 20
exercise: How many more adult teeth than baby teeth does a 13-year-old usually have, wisdom teeth not counted? | 8 | 28 | 20 | 48
exercise: Phelps won 28 Olympic medals, 23 of them gold. How many were not gold? | 5 | 23 | 51 | 3
test: «my heart's beating a million times a minute rn» after the 100 m. About how fast can a kid's heart really beat when running hard? | About 160 to 190 a minute | About a million a minute | About 1,000 a minute | About 20 a minute
test: Grandad: «Back in my day we counted our pulse for a whole minute, none of this times four». Lucy counts 24 in 15 seconds. Would Grandad's way give the same answer? | Yes, about 96 either way | No, his way gives 24 | No, it gives 384 | No, it would give 60
test: «chill, I only had a wee can of cola, it's nothing» says Eilidh from Glasgow. How does one can compare with her whole day's limit? | It's already more than the whole limit | It's about half of the day's sugar limit | It's about a quarter of the limit | It's well under the limit, so it's nothing
test: «Ugh this burn's been under the tap for ages, like an hour» — it went under at 4:05 and now it's 4:12. How long is left? | 13 more minutes | 8 minutes | 15 minutes | None left
test: Josh's mum: «he's had a head clash, but it's the cup final in two weeks, he'll be grand». What does the guidance say about the final? | He can't play it: at least 21 days off | He can play if he is fine by then | He can play if he wears a scrum cap | He can play the second half only
test: «Having a cola at 7 pm, bruv, I'll sleep fine by midnight». About how much caffeine is left at midnight? | About half of it | None, it's all worn off by then | About a quarter of it | All of it, nothing gone yet
test: Amir: «sun cream at 10, then I swam at 11 and towelled off, I'm sorted till 12». What's wrong? | Swimming and towelling mean put it on again now | Nothing, 2 hours haven't passed yet | Sun cream lasts all day once it's on | Sun cream only matters on hot, cloudless days
test: A class of 100 kids, and for herd immunity to measles 95 need to be immune. At most how many can be not immune? | 5 | 95 | 50 | 10
test: «Proper job!» shouts Dad: 2 tries, one converted, plus a drop goal worth 3. How many points did the team score? | 15 | 13 | 17 | 10
test: Tokyo «2020» was held in 2021. How many years after Tokyo did Paris 2024 come? | Only 3 years | 4 years | 5 years | 2 years
test: The World Cup kicks off at 7 pm in Los Angeles. Ellie in Leeds wants to watch it live. What time is that for her? | 3 am | 2 am | 11 pm | 7 pm
test: 48 teams start the 2026 World Cup and 32 get through the groups. How many go home after the groups? | 16 | 32 | 12 | 24
exam: Given a pulse count of 19 beats over a period of 15 seconds, determine the rate per minute. | 76 | 19 | 34 | 95
exam: A pupil's alarm is set for 7:00 am and eleven hours of sleep are required. State the latest time by which sleep should begin. | 8:00 pm | 9:00 pm | 7:00 pm | 6:00 pm
exam: Determine the total sugar, in grams, in three 330 ml cans of regular cola, each containing approximately 35 g. | About 105 g | About 72 g | About 35 g | About 99 g
exam: Of the 28 Olympic medals won by Michael Phelps, 3 were silver and 23 gold. Determine the number of bronze medals. | 2 | 5 | 3 | 1
